## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical integration of image provenance with runtime attestation, ensuring defense in depth for CNF deployments in multi-region clusters.

## Key Concepts
- Image signing with Cosign and KMS-backed keys
- SPDX SBOM association and SBOM validation
- In-cluster attestation service generating verifiable tokens
- Admission control enforcing both provenance and attestation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: basic attestation gate
function attest(imageDigest, token, sbom) {
  if (!verifySignature(imageDigest)) return false;
  if (!verifySBOM(sbom)) return false;
  if (!verifyToken(token)) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle key rotation and revocation in the KMS?
- How would you simulate attestation failures in a namespace to verify policy behavior?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a comprehensive cross-architecture supply chain security and runtime trust workflow that addresses edge deployment challenges, including offline scenarios and real-time policy enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- Per-architecture image signing and SBOM provenance tracking
- Runtime attestation with architecture-aware claim verification
- Policy enforcement using OPA Gatekeeper with architecture-specific constraints
- Edge connectivity management and canary-driven rollback mechanisms

## Code Example
```javascript
function isAllowed(image, arch) {
  // Verify Cosign signature for specific architecture
  const signatureValid = verifyCosignSignature(image, arch);
  const sbomPresent = checkSBOMPresence(image, arch);
  const attestationValid = verifyInTotoAttestation(image, arch);

  return signatureValid && sbomPresent && attestationValid;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical design of end-to-end attestation workflows in multi-tenant environments with integrated policy enforcement and security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Post-deployment tenant-scoped attestations using HSM-based key management
- SBOM integrity verification and runtime hashing for supply chain security
- OPA/Gatekeeper integration for policy validation and traffic gating
- Multi-tenant security isolation with compliance enforcement mechanisms

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sample attestation verification pseudocode
function verifyAttestation(attestation, tenantPolicy) {
  // Validate signature with tenant's HSM public key
  const isValidSignature = crypto.verify(
    attestation.signature,
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.publicKey
  );

  // Check policy compliance through OPA/Gatekeeper
  const isCompliant = opa.evaluate(
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.constraints
  );

  return isValidSignature && isCompliant;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to securely manage per-tenant TLS credentials in a CNF gateway, including secret-driven config, hot-reload of TLS material, and per-tenant mTLS verification.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes Secrets mounted as TLS material for sidecars
- Hot-reload of TLS credentials without pod restart
- Mutual TLS with per-tenant CA certificates
- Rotation cadence, error handling, and tenant isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo example: load TLS certs from mounted files and reload on change
let tlsContext = tls.createSecureContext({
  ca: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/ca.pem'),
  cert: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/cert.pem'),
  key: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/key.pem')
});

// watch secret mount and refresh TLS context
fs.watch('/mnt/cnf-tls', () => {
  tlsContext = tls.createSecureContext({
    ca: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/ca.pem'),
    cert: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/cert.pem'),
    key: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/key.pem')
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate certificate expiry and revocation in this flow?
- What are the trade-offs between in-cluster secret rotation vs external secret management (e.g., Vault) for CNF gateways?

